what this does and does not say:
  * the magnitude 47 and 48 call unpriced is priced. an access plan derived per element
    at runtime costs about 3.1 times one that is a compile-time constant, stable across
    four sizes spanning the L1 boundary, against a dense-carrier competitor arm.
  * it prices COMPILE TIME AGAINST RUNTIME, not derivation against site. a site holding
    the width and the strategy's rule as consts could reach the windowed number itself.
    what the bench bounds is the cost of the plan not being a const at all.
  * the windowed arm's plan is P = 8 / gcd(W, 8) fields per whole byte group. that gcd is
    the same phase-period fact p4 derives and 16:179-180 generalises wrongly from W=13.
    an independent instance of p4's finding, in committed harness code by another author.
